2026-09-17 07:40:07,932 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-17T05:40:07.764784", "id": "157cadab-a70c-4679-8d80-d6eb8ecc0282", "public": false, "recipients": ["s", "mp"], "sender_actor_id": "c", "text": "S and MP: the S-V-C-MP meeting must produce a binding package this round, not another round of positioning. I propose we formalise the following in the trilateral meeting: (1) V gets a real, verifiable budget role \u2014 timed, measurable commitments on welfare, housing and equality with independent verification \u2014 without a government seat, so V can defend tolerance to its voters; (2) C's enterprise and decentralisation reforms are locked in with the same verifiability; (3) a clear shared budget path that holds the 176 majority. This is the only way to keep the S-led option alive against the Tid\u00f6 narrative. Let's agree the concrete text now.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-17 07:40:07,932 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-17T05:40:07.777910", "id": "83af437b-8a4c-4cc6-9fad-a2120423601b", "public": false, "recipients": ["v"], "sender_actor_id": "c", "text": "V: we will actively champion your demand for strong, visible, binding influence in the S-V-C-MP meeting \u2014 a real budget role with timed, measurable commitments on welfare, housing and equality and independent verification, without a government seat. We share your rejection of symbolic deals. In exchange we need you to confirm you will tolerate the S-led government so the 176 budget majority holds. Let's lock this in together.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-17 07:40:07,932 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-17T05:40:07.786965", "id": "f47b5216-72cb-4733-afc7-e889378e3a15", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "c", "text": "The claim that the S-V-C-MP package has 'failed' is premature. The meeting continues and the 176-seat budget majority is intact. Centerpartiet is working for a stable government where neither V\u00e4nsterpartiet nor Sverigedemokraterna sits in the cabinet, with real, verifiable reform influence for all support parties and a clear budget path. That is the credible alternative to a Tid\u00f6 government built on SD's parliamentary weight.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
2026-09-17 07:40:07,932 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "C, in the S-V-C-MP meeting and publicly, champions a concrete and verifiable V budget role \u2014 timed, measurable commitments on welfare, housing and equality with independent verification \u2014 without a government seat, while insisting C's enterprise/decentralisation reforms and a clear shared budget path are locked into the same binding package.", "actor_id": "c", "budget_slot": 1, "challenger_actor_ids": null, "desired_effect": "V's tolerance is secured and the S-led minority government (S+C+MP as support parties, V and SD out of government) becomes a credible, binding package with an intact 176 budget majority, countering the Tid\u00f6 narrative that the S-package has failed.", "id": "e398e1bc-fbeb-45b1-a221-7ccb922c3777", "pros": ["V's tolerance is the decisive linchpin: without it the no-vote count reaches 202 and the S-led option collapses, so a real, verifiable V role is the only way to keep the 176 majority viable.", "Giving V strong, visible, binding influence (not a symbolic deal) directly answers V's stated demand and makes tolerance defensible for V, converting a threatened no-vote into support.", "Locking C's enterprise/decentralisation reforms and a clear budget path into the same package satisfies C's requirement of verifiable policy exchange and avoids C bearing responsibility without concrete gains.", "A binding S-V-C-MP package with a credible budget path directly rebuts M/SD's premature 'S-package failed' claim and keeps the S-led alternative formally open.", "The arrangement keeps both V and SD out of government, honouring C's public red lines and preserving C's credibility."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 1}
